  "content": "## Projects, deployments and domains\n\nResolve a team by slug, a project by name, and deployments by the observed\nproject id. Team ids start with `team_`, project ids with `prj_`, and deployment\nids with `dpl_`. A deployment hostname and a deployment id identify the same\ndeployment; an alias can later point to a different deployment.\n\nSome project paths accept a project name, but a deployment list's projectId\nfilter requires the observed `prj_` id. Resolve the name before listing its\ndeployments; an empty result for a guessed name does not prove absence.\nComplete each identifier lookup before starting the reads that depend on it.\n\nThe configured team is a routing default, not a restriction. Explicit teamId\nor slug selects another team the token can reach; teamId: null selects personal\nscope. Vercel token permissions determine access. Prefer an explicit team when\njoining resources across several calls.\n\nRead deployment state before its build events. Runtime logs diagnose requests\nafter a deployment built; build logs explain a failed build. Narrow time windows\nbefore raising collection limits. Generic reads refuse live follow streams;\nuse the bounded build/runtime readers. Deployment timestamps are milliseconds.\n\nProject domains and deployment aliases are different joins: a project domain\nbelongs to the project, while an alias identifies its assigned deployment.\nRead a pending domain's verification instructions before changing DNS.\n\n## Environment changes\n\nResolve environment-variable ids using metadata, including target, branch and\ncustom environment. A key can have distinct production and preview values.\nExisting values cannot be retrieved. Supply new values only when the task asks\nfor a change; confirm the returned id and metadata.\n\nEnvironment changes apply to future deployments. A new deployment is a separate\nwrite. Promoting an existing deployment does not rebuild it or update embedded\nenvironment values. After an uncertain update, reconcile observable metadata\nsuch as id, targets and comment; reading metadata cannot verify a secret value.\n\n## Explicit files and credentials\n\nDeployment files can reference previously uploaded digests. File uploads accept\nexplicit bytes and never read a path on the agent's machine. Decrypted-value,\ncredential-minting, protection-bypass-link, signing and domain move-out operations\nare refused; use Vercel's dashboard for those workflows.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** a paged `list_*` or `search_*` read takes `limit` (default 20, at most 100) and `cursor`. While `page.hasMore` is true, pass `page.nextCursor` back unchanged as `cursor`; the last page has no `nextCursor`.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `vercel_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `vercel_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `vercel_api_read` calls a reviewed read. `vercel_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused; these are refused by design: `GET /v1/env/{id}`, `GET /v1/global-config/{edgeConfigId}/backups/{edgeConfigBackupVersionId}`, `GET /v1/global-config/{edgeConfigId}/item/{edgeConfigItemKey}`, `GET /v1/global-config/{edgeConfigId}/items`, `GET /v1/global-config/{edgeConfigId}/token/{token}`, `GET /v1/global-config/{edgeConfigId}/tokens`, `GET /v1/installations/{integrationConfigurationId}/resources/{resourceId}/experimentation/global-config`, `GET /v1/projects/{idOrName}/env/{id}`, `GET /v1/registrar/domains/{domain}/auth-code`, `GET /v10/projects/{idOrName}/env`, `PATCH /aliases/{id}/protection-bypass`, `PATCH /v1/projects/{idOrName}/protection-bypass`, `POST /api-keys`, `POST /projects/{idOrName}/transfer-request`, `POST /v1/connect/authorize/{connector}`, `POST /v1/connect/token/{connector}`, `POST /v1/global-config/{edgeConfigId}/token`, `POST /v1/installations/{integrationConfigurationId}/credentials/rotate`, `POST /v1/integrations/sso/token`, `POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/sign/message`, `POST /v1/kms/issuers/{issuerId}/sign/token`, `POST /v1/projects/traces/session`, `POST /v1/projects/{idOrName}/avatar`, `POST /v1/projects/{idOrName}/token`, `POST /v2/files`, `POST /v3/user/tokens`, `PUT /v1/projects/{projectIdOrName}/feature-flags/sdk-keys`, `PUT /v8/artifacts/{hash}`.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. `not_found` means the record does not exist; this API tells absence from a permission gap. It documents no conflict.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
